	(text "pixel mode pipeline:	(2 cycles wide)\n	(consider the following happening 'in parallel')\n	- fetched pixels are latched;\n	- rams start fetching the next 2 pixels;\n	- the latched pixels are shown multiplexed\n	by col-counter's bit 0.\n\ncharacters mode pipeline:	(8 cycles wide)\n	- fetched bitmap byte (by rom) is latched;\n	- rams start fetching the character word;\n	- rom starts fetching the bitmap once the\n	rams are done (by using the fetched word's\n	ascii code & line-counter's bits 0..2, as address);\n	- color circuit generates the foreground\n	& background colors from the character\n	word's color byte;\n	- fetched bitmap is shown multiplexed by\n	col-counter's bits 0..2.\n\nBecause the shown pixels are delayed by 2 clock cycles\nfrom the counters, the sync signals are triggered using\na 'jkclk' (clock for the jk flip flops) whose frequency\nis a fraction of the original clock.\nIn the case of the pixel mode, jkclk's freq. should be\nclk/2, while in characters mode, clk/8."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 379.984 58.674 0)
